Moore's Voting Algorithm

Time Complexity:
O(n)

Space Complexity:
O(1)

Approach:
1. Initialize majority_ele and count = 0
2. Traverse the array once
3. If count becomes 0, choose the current element as the candidate
4. If current element matches the candidate, increment count
5. Otherwise decrement count
6. Continue this process for all elements
7. At the end, the remaining candidate is the majority element




class Solution {
    public int majorityElement(int[] nums) {
        int majority_ele = 0;
        int count = 0;
        for(int i=0; i<nums.length; i++){
            if(count == 0){
                majority_ele = nums[i];
            }
            if(majority_ele != nums[i]){
                count--;
            }
            else{
                count++;
            }
        }
        return majority_ele;
    }
}
